To minimize the total distance, reflect point \(B\) across the wall segment to a virtual point \(B'\). The shortest path from \(A\) to the wall that touches the wall and then goes to \(B\) is a straight line from \(A\) to \(B'\). Reflecting \(B\) across the wall (distance \(500\)) adds an extra \(1200\) horizontal distance (the length of the wall), placing \(B'\) at \((1200,500)\).

The reflected distance is
\[
d = \sqrt{(1200-0)^2 + (500-300)^2}
= \sqrt{1200^2 + 200^2}
= \sqrt{144\cdot10000 + 40000}
= \sqrt{1440000 + 40000}
= \sqrt{1480000}
= 100\sqrt{148}
= 200\sqrt{37}.
\]

Numerically,
\[
200\sqrt{37} \approx 200 \times 6.0828 \approx 1216.56\text{ m}.
\]

Rounded to the nearest meter, the minimum distance is \(1217\) meters.
